  "summary": "The Trecento ( tray-CHEN-toh, US also  treh-, Italian: [treˈtʃɛnto]; short for milletrecento, \"1300\") refers to the 14th century in Italian cultural history.",
  "description": "The Trecento ( tray-CHEN-toh, US also  treh-, Italian: [treˈtʃɛnto]; short for milletrecento, \"1300\") refers to the 14th century in Italian cultural history. The Trecento is considered to be the beginning of the Italian Renaissance or at least the Proto-Renaissance in art history. The Trecento was also famous as a time of heightened literary activity, with writers working in the vernacular instead of Latin. In music, the Trecento was a time of vigorous activity in Italy, as it was in France, with which there was a frequent interchange of musicians and influences.",
